# LARAVEL CONVENTIONS
- Generate with `php artisan make:*` (model -mfs, controller --resource, request, policy, seeder, test, job, mail).
- Laravel 11+: no `app/Console/Kernel.php`. Middleware/exceptions/schedule live in `bootstrap/app.php` and `routes/console.php`.
- Use `config('...')`, never `env()` outside config files.
- Thin controllers -> FormRequest for validation -> Service/Action class for business logic -> Eloquent models.
- Authorization via Policies + Gates for every controller action (RBAC at server level, NFR-SEC-003). Never rely on hidden buttons.
- Route model binding; named routes (`leads.index`, `leads.convert`); group by module with `->middleware('auth')`.
- Eager load (`with()`) to avoid N+1; paginate lists (default 25, hard max 200 - NFR-SCAL-002).
- Wrap multi-step operations (lead conversion, clone, bulk owner change, import) in `DB::transaction()`.
- Use Eloquent/Query Builder bindings only - no string-concatenated SQL (NFR-SEC-004).
- Emails, reminders, digests, report subscriptions: queued Jobs/Mailables + scheduler, never inline in requests.
- Use a shared `HasAuditFields` trait (created_by, updated_by) and Laravel timestamps on every business table.
- Return flash messages (`with('success', ...)`) for toasts; JSON only from dedicated `/api` or AJAX endpoints.
- Code style: PSR-12, run `./vendor/bin/pint` before every commit.
